          deckDescription: 'A standard 52-card French deck; no jokers. Pedro Sancho is a trick-taking variant. The high bidder chooses the trump suit; within that suit the 5 (pedro) and 9 (sancho) are scoring cards worth 5 and 9 points. The other 5 is not a trump. Full deck used for four players.',
          suitDescription: 'The four French suits (hearts, diamonds, clubs, spades) each have thirteen cards. The high bidder names one suit as trump; in that suit only, the 5 (pedro) and 9 (sancho) have extra point value. Suit and rank determine trick value and following rules.',
          rankDescription: 'Standard ranks Ace through King. In the chosen trump suit the 5 is pedro (5 points) and the 9 is sancho (9 points). Trump ranking A,K,Q,J,10,9,8,7,6,5,4,3,2. Trick order: highest trump wins, else highest card of led suit.',
